g it all.","published":"2026-11-22T01:42:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Brandon's two TD runs lift No. 9 Tennessee past LSU","description":"Tennessee's stifling defense shut down LSU, and the No. 9 Volunteers beat the Tigers 27-13 on Saturday to maintain their place in the College Football Playoff hunt.","published":"2026-11-22T01:48:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556758/brandon-two-td-runs-lift-no-9-tennessee-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bryce Underwood makes most of second chance, sparks Michigan's upset of UCLA","description":"Reinserted as Michigan's starting quarterback earlier this week, Bryce Underwood threw a 3-yard 2-point conversion pass Jalen Hoffman, lifting the Wolverines to an 18-16 triple-overtime win over previously unbeaten No. 4 UCLA on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T01:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556702/bryce-underwood-michigan-outlast-ucla-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T01:12:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana's CFP hopes take hit after OT loss at Washington","description":"Indiana might not get a chance to defend its national championship after losing 27-24 at Washington on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:30:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556327/indiana-cfp-hopes-take-hit-ot-loss-washington","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA loses Ty Dieffenbach to injury, stays resolute with B1G title game in reach","description":"UCLA coach Bob Chesney said his message to the Bruins was, \"Nobody hang your head,\" despite losing QB Ty Dieffenbach to injury in a tough, 18-16 defeat at Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:41:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556107/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-carted-3ot-loss-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T00:47:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Preseason No. 1 Ohio State suffers fourth loss, will 'evaluate what's going on'","description":"For coach Ryan Day and his Ohio State Buckeyes, the dream of a College Football Playoff run is dead, as the preseason No. 1 team in college football lost its fourth game on Saturday afternoon, a 31-28 decision at the hands of the Nebraska Cornhuskers.","published":"2026-11-22T00:30:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50555411/preseason-no-1-ohio-state-sees-cfp-hopes-end-4th-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4941011/john-nestor","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Nestor_(American_football)"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"John Nestor (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Nestor_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:29Z","intro":"John Nestor (born May 13, 2005) is an American football cornerback for the Minnesota Golden Gophers. He previously played for the Iowa Hawkeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Nestor attended Marist High School in Chicago, Illinois. Coming out of high school, he was rated as a three-star recruit by 247Sports and committed to play college football for the Iowa Hawkeyes over offers from other schools such as Iowa State, Minnesota, Purdue, and Kansas."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"IOWA\nAs a freshman in 2023, Nestor played sparingly, but entered the 2024 season with an expanded role. He appeared in ten games that season, recording 14 tackles and a fumble recovery, after which he entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nMINNESOTA\nNestor transferred to play for the Minnesota Golden Gophers. In week 2 of the 2025 season, he notched two interceptions, one of which he returned 29 yards for a touchdown, in a victory over Northwestern State. Nestor was named the Big Ten Defensive Player of the Week following a win over Wisconsin in the regular season finale, recording nine tackles with two being for a loss, two interceptions, and a fumble recovery."}]}}